  "notes": "KANJI NOTE:\n{播|は} means \"to sow\" or \"to spread.\" This is a relatively uncommon kanji.\n\nAGRICULTURAL TERMS:\n- {播種|はしゅ} - sowing, seeding\n- {発芽|はつが} - germination\n- {苗|なえ} - seedling\n- {定植|ていしょく} - transplanting\n\nMEDICAL USAGE:\nIn oncology, {播種|はしゅ} refers to cancer spreading to body cavities like the {腹膜|ふくまく} (peritoneum). This is different from {転移|てんい} (metastasis) through the bloodstream or lymphatic system.",
